    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d890">

                <pb facs="1020" n="908" xml:id="pg908"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.6363 Manchuria/182: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Japan</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-04-26T20:00:00-05:00">April 26, 1935—8 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>68. Your 93, April 26, 5 p.m. Representatives of Standard-Vacuum plan to call at
                    Department April 29 for further discussion.</p>
                <p>Meanwhile, in the light of Department’s views as set forth in penultimate
                    paragraph of its 67, April 24, 7 p.m., you should make no commitment to any
                    other line of procedure.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
